module bindings.rust.raw_pointer_from_temporary;

// A raw pointer taken from a value that the same statement created and then
// dropped. The Rust shape is a borrow-style pointer accessor -- as_ptr or
// as_mut_ptr -- called on the result of a try expression:
//
//     let ptr = make_thing(arg)?.as_ptr();
//     use_later(ptr);
//
// The `?` unwraps the Result or Option into a temporary whose drop runs when
// the let statement ends, and the raw pointer handed to the later use points
// into freed memory. Raw pointers carry no lifetime, so the borrow checker
// cannot object; this is the class clippy pins for its one notorious spelling
// (temporary_cstring_as_ptr) and it recurs with any owned buffer type whose
// constructor returns Result. Returning the pointer to a caller, or passing it
// to a foreign function after the statement, is use after free.
//
// The fix is to bind the value to a local first, so the pointee outlives the
// pointer's uses; every as_ptr in the function then reads a named, still-live
// binding.
//
// The discriminator is the try operator directly in front of the borrow, read
// from the function's compacted body text. The call tokens cannot carry it:
// the frontend lowers as_ptr on any receiver that is not a name to the same
// `?.as_ptr` call path whether the receiver is a dropped temporary or
// compile-time constant data (`concat!(file!(), "\0").as_ptr()` points at
// static storage and is safe), and a pointer consumed inside its own
// statement -- passed as an argument before the semicolon -- is safe too,
// because Rust keeps the temporary alive until the statement completes. The
// `?.as_ptr` spelling narrows to the one receiver form whose pointee is always
// a fresh temporary: the try expression materializes a new value, so a pointer
// kept past the statement always dangles.
binding rawPointerFromTemporary {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "rust" and containsAny(node.token, [")?.as_ptr(", ")?.as_mut_ptr("])
  emit issue code.RawPointerFromTemporary at node
}
